MID_SE_Ism_Yan_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Ism_Yan_A_001: Hey! What the— Get away from me!
MID_SE_Ism_Yan_A_002: <NCA>"What's going on?"
MID_SE_Ism_Yan_A_003: But I just heard you saying you wished you were\ndead. What am I to do but fulfill your request?
MID_SE_Ism_Yan_A_004: No! Why are you doing this?!
MID_SE_Ism_Yan_A_005: <NCA>"Stop this, NOW!"
MID_SE_Ism_Yan_A_006: H-help me! Please!
MID_SE_Ism_Yan_A_007: Now, did you hear yourself? Just now, you cried\nout for help. Your desire to live is strong.
MID_SE_Ism_Yan_A_008: Your words yearned for death. Your heart yearns for\nlife. The world seeks to break us. Don't let it.
MID_SE_Ism_Yan_A_009: Here—eat this. Rid yourself of hunger. That will\nrestore your natural fortitude.
MID_SE_Ism_Yan_A_010: Th-thank you! I'll hold on to life, I promise! W-with\nboth hands!
MID_SE_Ism_Yan_A_011: Ah! If it isn't the Promised One. Care to join me\nfor a bite?
MID_SE_Ism_Yan_A_012: <NCA>"You were...trying to help him?"
MID_SE_Ism_Yan_A_013: Not at all! I overheard the poor wretch saying that\nhe wished he was dead. I thought I'd oblige.
MID_SE_Ism_Yan_A_014: Though I'll admit, I knew that deep down he truly\nwanted to live.
MID_SE_Ism_Yan_A_015: The gods make our world tumultuous. Some lose\ntheir minds in the maelstrom...and speak madness.
MID_SE_Ism_Yan_A_016: <NCA>"Your method was too extreme."
MID_SE_Ism_Yan_A_017: <NCB>"That was reckless of you."
MID_SE_Ism_Yan_A_018: <ACA>I believe one's methods must be as extreme as the\npain one is trying to alleviate.
MID_SE_Ism_Yan_A_019: <ACB>Hahaha! Perhaps! A reckless bent always came\nmore naturally to me than moderation!
MID_SE_Ism_Yan_A_020: I am a man who abandoned his gods and their\ntemples. Maybe the mad one...is me.
MID_SE_Ism_Yan_A_021: <NCA>"Why did you abandon it all?"
MID_SE_Ism_Yan_A_022: I'm sorry to say those memories are lost to me.\nI cast off my past, wherever I wander.
MID_SE_Ism_Yan_A_023: But I do know that what I believe in—on this\nday—is what I did back then.
MID_SE_Ism_Yan_A_024: Those who want to live their life must be allowed to.\nWithout fear, without neglect. No matter what.
MID_SE_Ism_Yan_S: <EDH>
MID_SE_Ism_Yan_S_001: Good grief. How long must I wait? You're a terrible\nguest of honor—the worst! Hahaha!
MID_SE_Ism_Yan_S_002: Aha! Promised One, old friend! So, you made it\nout safe! You're just in time for a drink...
MID_SE_Ism_Yan_S_003: <NCA>"Are you...drunk?"
MID_SE_Ism_Yan_S_004: Oh, I've had one or two! I've been toasting\nyou, the one who saved the world!
MID_SE_Ism_Yan_S_005: Many, many people were here, raising drink after\ndrink in your honor. It went on forever...
MID_SE_Ism_Yan_S_006: Until it was just me. But now you're here in the\nnick of time for your toast.
MID_SE_Ism_Yan_S_007: <NCA>"You've been waiting here the whole time?"
MID_SE_Ism_Yan_S_008: Where else? I suspected we'd all see you right\nhere if we waited long enough.
MID_SE_Ism_Yan_S_009: Come on, come on... Let's have that drink. I'll call\neveryone back. It'll be a party for the ages!
MID_SE_Ism_Yan_S_010: <NCA>"I really shouldn't..."
MID_SE_Ism_Yan_S_011: Bah, you're no fun. Do you good to cut loose\nonce in a while...
MID_SE_Ism_Yan_S_012: Fine, fine. I'll let you be. Just glad you made it\nhere safe and sound.
MID_SE_Ism_Yan_S_013: Ah... Well, it's time I moved on anyway, now that\nyou're here. My life of wandering calls...
MID_SE_Ism_Yan_S_014: The war has ended, thanks to you. But many people\nout there—everywhere—still need rescue.
MID_SE_Ism_Yan_S_015: We can't ignore those who are suffering, can we,\nPromised One?
MID_SE_Ism_Yan_S_016: <NCA>"I'll wander with you."
MID_SE_Ism_Yan_S_017: <NCB>"Let's save people together."
MID_SE_Ism_Yan_S_018: I expected you'd say that. We are of like mind...\nin some ways.
MID_SE_Ism_Yan_S_019: But I must go my own path. To those in need,\nI offer a promise different from yours.
MID_SE_Ism_Yan_S_020: We will each save lives on our journeys.
MID_SE_Ism_Yan_S_021: <RSDS>But always remember, the world changes, people\nchange. Life itself wanders.
MID_SE_Ism_Yan_S_022: Let us live our lives, Promised One. Perhaps my\nwandering will wend its way back to you...in time.